.TH GPS-TOF-EXPORT-FIGURES 1 "2026-11-06" "gps-tof 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
export_figures.py \- export the schematic figures as standalone SVG and PNG files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 scripts/export_figures.py
[\fB\-\-html\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-scale\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-png\fR] [\fB\-\-chrome\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads every \fB<figure>\fR SVG in \fIdocs/nova-schematic.html\fR (the plan, elevation and
transverse views and the Near Detector front face), resolves the page's CSS tokens
(currentColor, var(--beam), ...) to the light-theme colours, embeds a style block and a white
background, and writes one standalone SVG per figure.  Each SVG is then rasterised to a PNG
with headless Chrome/Chromium at \fIscale\fR pixels per SVG unit.  Files are named
\fINN-title.svg\fR / \fI.png\fR in the output directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-html " FILE"
Page to read (default \fIdocs/nova-schematic.html\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " DIR"
Output directory (default \fIdocs/figures\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
PNG resolution, pixels per SVG unit (default 2: a 900x400 figure becomes 1800x800).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-png
Write the SVGs only.
.TP
.BI \-\-chrome " PATH"
Chrome or Chromium executable (default: the macOS application path, then google-chrome,
chromium, chromium-browser, chrome on the PATH).
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
    python3 scripts/export_figures.py                  # docs/figures/01-plan-view.svg/.png ...
    python3 scripts/export_figures.py --scale 4 --out /tmp/fig
.fi
.SH FILES
.I docs/figures/
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gps-tof (1)
